# Mutant 09 — R-CLICK-2
# Description: when the country header appears more than once, the first value is used instead of
#   recording `unknown`. The Referer duplicate rule (R-CLICK-1) is untouched.
# Why realistic: `headers.get(name)` is the idiomatic one-liner; the "appears more than once" clause is
#   an unusual requirement that is easy to drop while tidying the function.
# Trigger: GET /{code} with two `cf-ipcountry: US` headers (or `US` and `DE`) -> topCountries shows US
#   instead of unknown.

